    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209-a9">

                <pb facs="0562" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg540"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9 in No. 74.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Earl
                            Granville.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 28,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I received at 8 o’clock this evening
                    your note of this date, in which you say you think it desirable to address to
                    me, as you therein proceed to do, some observations in addition to what is
                    stated in your letter of yesterday.</p>
                <p>I shall hasten to-night to communicate the whole of this note by telegraph to my
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, my Lord, your Lordship’s,
                    most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBT. C. SCHENCK.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
